-- title:
--   Weight-2m cusp forms from integrality over ℂ[j] and ℂ[1/j]
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $m\ge 1$ be a natural number. Write $J :=$ [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb ℂ ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) for the image in $\mathbb C((q))$, under the coefficientwise ring map induced by $\mathbb Q\to\mathbb C$, of the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the power series } j_{\mathrm{Num}}$ over $\mathbb Q)$, and let $\vartheta$ denote the $\mathbb C$-linear operator [`ModularCurve.thetaL`](def/ModularCurve_QExpansionDiff.html#L16) on $\mathbb C((q))$ sending $f$ to $q\cdot f'$. Let $X$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb C$ lying in [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ (ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull N)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, in the intermediate field of $\mathbb C((q))/\mathbb C$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series $q$-expanded along the divisors $d\mid N$ of $j$. Let $M$ be a natural number, and assume: (i) $X^{6}J^{4m}(J-1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $\mathbb C$-subalgebra of $\mathbb C((q))$ generated by $J$; (ii) $X^{2M}J^{mM+1}(J-1728)^{mM}$ is integral over the $\mathbb C$-subalgebra generated by $J^{-1}$. Then there exists a cusp form $f$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ of weight $2m$ whose $q$-expansion of width $1$, regarded as a Laurent series, equals $X\cdot(\vartheta J)^{m}$.
--
--   This is the analytic criterion recognising an element of the field of modular functions of level $N$, multiplied by $(\vartheta j)^m$, as the $q$-expansion of a weight-$2m$ cusp form on $\Gamma_0(N)$, the two integrality hypotheses encoding holomorphy on the upper half-plane and the vanishing conditions at the cusps. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral), and rests on the criterion [`ModularForm.exists_cuspForm_mul_eq_of_analyticOrderAt_le`](thm.html#ModularForm.exists_cuspForm_mul_eq_of_analyticOrderAt_le) together with the order and growth estimates supplied by the two integrality assumptions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral.lean

